                                {
                                    "id": "metabc",
                                    "elType": "widget",
                                    "widgetType": "text-editor",
                                    "settings": {
                                        "editor": "<p style=\"margin:0 0 14px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#3D4F66\"><a href=\"https://dev.biopentra.eu/\" style=\"color:#1F5FAE;text-decoration:none\">Home</a> &gt; Resources &gt; Metabolic Research Peptides</p>",
                                        "text_color": "#3D4F66"
                                    },
                                    "elements": []
                                },
                                {
                                    "id": "metaH1",
                                    "elType": "widget",
                                    "widgetType": "heading",
                                    "settings": {
                                        "header_size": "h1",
                                        "title": "Metabolic Research Peptides",
                                        "title_color": "#0F1F33"
                                    },
                                    "elements": []
                                },
                                {
                                    "id": "metaintro",
                                    "elType": "widget",
                                    "widgetType": "text-editor",
                                    "settings": {
                                        "editor": "<p style=\"margin:0 0 14px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#3D4F66\">Metabolic research peptides are peptide-based materials commonly discussed in laboratory work focused on metabolic signaling. Research in this area often examines how peptide messages relate to energy balance, glucose response models, and broader endocrine signaling networks under controlled conditions.</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 14px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#3D4F66\">Rather than describing a single molecule type, the category brings together compounds that appear in similar experimental conversations\u2014particularly where peptide signaling models are used to study pathway behavior, receptor interaction, or measured metabolic markers in assays.</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 14px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#3D4F66\">On a research storefront, a metabolic peptide resource page helps connect related catalog entries, clarify shared terminology, and situate individual products within a consistent laboratory frame. Readers can use this page before reviewing specific listings or adjacent guides on storage, intended use, and other peptide categories.</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 14px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#3D4F66\">This overview from BioPentra explains how metabolic research peptides are grouped in research commerce and literature, links to related catalog entries, and points to handling guidance for lyophilized research materials. It is educational content for laboratory research contexts only.</p>",
                                        "text_color": "#3D4F66"
                                    },
                                    "elements": []
                                }
                            ],
                            "isInner": true
                        }
                    ],
                    "isInner": true
